content.text:
Here’s the same idea with concrete call shapes.

## Success: always Kit types

### Create / get

```ts
const sandbox = await client.create({
  name: "kit-example",
  source: { image: { reference: "blaxel/base-image:latest" } },
});

// Kit SandboxInfo — not a raw @blaxel/core Sandbox
sandbox.id;            // "kit-example"
sandbox.provider;      // "blaxel"
sandbox.state;         // SandboxState enum (e.g. Queued / Running)
sandbox.providerState; // string from Blaxel ("DEPLOYED", …)
sandbox.resources?.memoryMib; // bigint | undefined
```

```go
instance, err := client.Create(ctx, &sandbox.CreateOptions{
    Name: sandbox.Value("kit-example"),
    Source: &sandbox.SandboxSource{Kind: &sandbox.Image{
        Image: &sandbox.ImageSource{Reference: "blaxel/base-image:latest"},
    }},
})
info := instance.Info()
// info.Id, info.Provider, info.State, info.ProviderState — Kit SandboxInfo
```

Under the hood Blaxel returns a native sandbox object; the provider maps it with `mapSandboxInfo` / `sandboxInfo` before you see it.

### Process

```ts
const result = await sandbox.process.run({ argv: ["false"] });

// Kit ExecResult — success even when exit ≠ 0
result.exitCode; // 1
result.stdout;   // Uint8Array
result.stderr;   // Uint8Array
// does NOT throw because exitCode is 1
```

```go
result, err := instance.Process().Run(ctx, &sandbox.ExecOptions{
    Argv: []string{"false"},
})
// err == nil; result.ExitCode == 1
```

Blaxel’s process response (`status`, `pid`, …) is translated into Kit `ExecResult` only.

### Filesystem

```ts
const bytes = await sandbox.filesystem.readFile("/tmp/a.txt"); // Uint8Array
const info  = await sandbox.filesystem.stat("/tmp/a.txt");
// info: { name, path, type: FileType.File, size, … } — Kit FileInfo
```

---

## Errors: always Kit `SandboxError`

### Known Blaxel code → specific kind

```ts
try {
  await client.create({ name: "kit-example", source: { image: { reference: "…" } } });
  await client.create({ name: "kit-example", source: { image: { reference: "…" } } });
} catch (e) {
  // e instanceof SandboxError
  e.kind;         // ErrorKind.AlreadyExists
  e.provider;     // "blaxel"
  e.operation;    // "create"
  e.providerCode; // "SANDBOX_ALREADY_EXISTS"
  e.statusCode;   // e.g. 409 if present
  e.cause;        // original @blaxel/core error
}
```

```go
err := … // second Create with same name
var se *sandbox.Error
errors.As(err, &se)
// se.Kind == ErrorKindAlreadyExists
// se.Provider == "blaxel"
// se.Operation == "create"
// *se.ProviderCode == "SANDBOX_ALREADY_EXISTS"
```

### Known HTTP status when code is missing

```ts
// Blaxel returns 504 with no useful code
e.kind;       // ErrorKind.Timeout
e.statusCode; // 504
e.provider;   // "blaxel"
e.operation;  // "run"
```

### Kit validation (never hits Blaxel)

```ts
await client.create({
  name: "Bad_Name",
  source: { image: { reference: "blaxel/base-image:latest" } },
});
// SandboxError
// kind: InvalidArgument
// field: "name"
// message: "sandbox-kit blaxel: name must be lowercase alphanumeric…"
```

```ts
await sandbox.filesystem.makeDirectory("/a/b", { parents: false });
// kind: Unsupported, field: "parents"
```

### Unknown Blaxel failure — still Kit, kind = Unknown

```ts
// New Blaxel code "SOME_NEW_CODE" not in the map, no mapped status
e.kind;         // ErrorKind.Unknown
e.provider;     // "blaxel"
e.operation;    // "refresh"
e.providerCode; // "SOME_NEW_CODE"  (preserved when present)
e.message;      // native message
e.cause;        // still the raw error for debugging
```

You still `catch (SandboxError)` / `errors.As(..., *sandbox.Error)` — you do **not** need to import `@blaxel/core` error types.

### Cancel

```ts
const ac = new AbortController();
ac.abort();
await sandbox.process.run({ argv: ["sleep", "60"] }, { signal: ac.signal });
// kind: Canceled
```

```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithCancel(ctx)
cancel()
_, err := instance.Process().Run(ctx, &sandbox.ExecOptions{Argv: []string{"sleep", "60"}})
// ErrorKindCanceled
```

---

## Mental model

```text
Your app
   │
   ▼
Kit Client  ──success──►  SandboxInfo | ExecResult | FileInfo | bytes
   │
   ├── Kit validation fail ──► SandboxError (field set)
   │
   └── Blaxel SDK fail ──map──► SandboxError (kind from code/status, else Unknown)
```

**App code only needs the Kit interface.** Raw Blaxel successes and failures are translated at the provider boundary before they reach you.

